Emerging Opportunities
Waste-to-Energy and Landfill Gas Recovery
Landfills and wastewater treatment plants offer opportunities to capture methane that might otherwise escape into the atmosphere or remain underutilized. Membrane-based upgrading can help convert recovered gas into a usable energy resource, supporting waste management and energy recovery initiatives.

Modular Systems for Decentralized Facilities
Compact membrane units can be suitable for distributed biogas projects where space, operational simplicity, and scalability are important. Modular system designs may help smaller facilities expand capacity as gas production increases.

Advanced Materials and Predictive Maintenance
New membrane materials and improved monitoring systems could help operators maintain separation performance and identify operating problems earlier. Collaboration among membrane manufacturers, engineering contractors, and biogas developers may accelerate the deployment of more efficient purification systems.

